    DECISION (no separate rationale or reopen-if cell; 4 cells): "**F-DG6-147: a live-selection export start no longer assembles the report in the request (ADR-0046 §2 is amended).** BE-Y4 measured the cause: about 55 % of the start is report assembly, which ADR-0046 §2 puts in the request. Trimming it (BE-Y4) did not bring 50 simultaneous starts under 2 s. **Decided:** (1) `createExport` for a live selection validates, authorizes and runs the restricted-source check **synchronously, so D-199's 403 is unchanged**. It then writes the job with its stored selection, its progress and its audit event, and answers 202 with no snapshot yet. (2) A durable API-process snapshot watch, following the connector-run-watch precedent (the assembler is API code, ADR-0002 rule 5), claims pending jobs `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. It re-checks the requester's access, assembles and writes the snapshot, and only then writes the `export_job.requested` outbox event for the worker. Access lost in between gives a failed job with an `errorCode` and en/ar text, never a file. (3) Contract: `ExportJob.snapshotId` is nullable until it is assigned, and an idempotent replay compares the stored selection. (4) Migration 0124 (snapshot nullable while pending, the selection column, a CHECK); the seed free-id example moves to 0125. (5) Exports of an existing snapshot are unchanged. The snapshot's data-as-of is the assembly time, recorded on the snapshot as before. Owners: T-DG6-BE-Y5 implements; T-DG6-ARCH-11 amends ADR-0046 §2 and ADR-0058 §7 and the data dictionary. Devops then re-measures the full dataset on the merged tree (T-DG6-DO-Y2), with `EXPORT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE` s…"
